# List the exercises. Start the API with Aspire first, then send "Create an account" once.
@host = http://localhost:5279

### Create an account → 201. The requests below use its access token.
# @name createAccount
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user-{{$guid}}@example.com",
  "password": "password",
  "timeZone": "Europe/Zagreb"
}

### Every exercise → 200. A new account has none.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Search in any case → 200.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/exercises?search=BENCH
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### One group → 200. Empty for a group that does not exist.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/exercises?groupId=0198a000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### A group that is not an ID → 400.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/exercises?groupId=not-an-id
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Not signed in → 401 unauthorized.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/exercises
